---
import { existsSync } from 'node:fs';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The CV link only appears once public/cv.pdf exists.
const hasCV = existsSync('./public/cv.pdf');

// Not on the page yet, add when ready: senior thesis, exotic 7-spheres paper, SHUR code,
// Math 72 Lie algebras paper + slides (PDFs already in public/papers/).
---
<Base title="Ribhu Hooja">
  <header class="intro">
    <img class="photo" src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo of Ribhu Hooja" width="450" height="600" />
    <div>
      <h1>Ribhu Hooja</h1>
      <p>
        I am a fourth-year undergraduate math major at Dartmouth College. My research interests are in
        Floer homology, low-dimensional topology, and spectral geometry. I'm drawn to the idea of using
        analytic invariants to study the topology and geometry of a space.
      </p>
      <p class="links">
        <a href="mailto:ribhu.hooja.27@dartmouth.edu">ribhu.hooja.27@dartmouth.edu</a><br />
        {hasCV && <><a href="/cv.pdf">CV</a> · </>}
        <a href="https://github.com/ribhuhooja">GitHub</a><br />
      <a href="https://ribhuhooja.xyz">Blog</a> - Some informal math writings</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <h2>Research</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/papers/shur-writeup-provisional.pdf">τ and ϵ invariants of generalized Mazur patterns</a> (in progress)<br />
      with Sean Kim, Filip Rupchin, Shreya Sinha, and Allison Tsypin
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Writing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/papers/lefschetz-fixed-point-talk.pdf">The Lefschetz fixed-point theorem</a> - Notes for a lecture in a graduate seminar on the Weil conjectures, Math 150, winter 2026. </li>
    <li><a href="/papers/m121-generic-smoothness-worksheet.pdf">Tangents, cotangents, derivations and differentials</a> - An expository worksheet on commutative algebra, Math 121, spring 2026. (<a href="/papers/m121-generic-smoothness-solutions.pdf">Solutions</a>)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Talks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><em>Satellite operations and bordered Heegaard Floer homology</em>. Dartmouth Topology Seminar, September 24, 2026.</li>
    <li><em>Sunada's method: using group theory to construct isospectral drums</em>. HRUMC, April 25, 2026. (<a href="/papers/HRUMC_Sunadas_Method_slides.pdf">Slides</a>)</li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; align-items: flex-start; }
  .photo { width: 160px; height: auto; border-radius: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .intro h1 { margin-top: 0; }
  .links { line-height: 1.8; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
